   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Answering with modesty",
     "texto": [
      "**A/V-기는요** can be used as a reply to turn down or downplay a compliment or an assumption: 잘하다 → **잘하기는요** (Not at all, I'm not that good at it), 좋다 → **좋기는요** (Not at all, it's not that good). The nuance depends on the conversation.",
      "잘하기는요. 아직 배울 게 많아요 = Not at all, I still have a lot to learn."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "It is not the same as -기는 하지만",
     "texto": [
      "At the end of a reply, **-기는요** corrects or minimises what the other person has just said. **-기는 하지만** concedes something and continues with a contrast: 읽기는 했지만 끝까지 못 읽었어요 = I did read it, but I could not finish it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
